  "about": "Field-testing record for the mainframe fact channels (docs/language_status/cics_field_testing.md, generated by tests/tools/field_testing.py). `estates` is every estate the engine has been checked against: kind public (a pinned corpus in corpora.json, keyed and censused) or private (a customer estate: an anonymised label only -- no code, names or paths in this repo), in the order they were first checked (`round`). `defects` is every ENGINE or FORGE defect a round exposed (and every census-brief gap): the ledger forgets a defect once it is fixed, so this log is its memory. Key errors are not logged here: field_testing.py counts them from each key's census rulings (key_fixed). severity: `fact` = a fact wrong, missing or extra (the skeleton changes); `attribute` = a fact's secondary attribute (a line number, a label). side: engine | forge | key | brief. Every entry cites its issue and/or fixing PR. `fields` gives each ledger field the PR that introduced it and `development_rounds`: how many of the round-ordered estates it was built or tuned against. Those rounds count toward 'tested on' but are NOT fresh: only a round after them tests the field on unseen code, and only fresh rounds can make a field field-tested. zopeneditor, CBSA and CardDemo were in language-crucible and the #3120 refraction corpora before the ledger existed, so they are development rounds for every channel.",
